

# 1. Introduction

This paper presents a comprehensive study on the impact of climate change on global agricultural productivity over the past three decades. The research aims to analyze how various climatic factors have influenced crop yields and food security worldwide.

## 1.1 Research Objectives

The primary objectives of this study are:

- To assess the relationship between temperature changes and crop yield variations.
- To evaluate the role of precipitation patterns in shaping agricultural output.
- To identify regions most vulnerable to climate-induced agricultural challenges.
- To propose sustainable strategies for enhancing resilience in farming communities.

## 1.2 Scope and Limitations

The scope of this study covers major cereal crops (wheat, rice, maize) across five continents. Data from 1990 to 2020 will be analyzed using statistical models and satellite imagery. Limitations include data availability gaps in certain developing countries and potential biases in historical records.

